-- title:
--   Vélu quotient of the Tate curve over a non-toric slot set
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a natural number with $p \neq 0$ and $p$ odd, $\zeta$ a unit of $K$ with $\zeta^{p}=1$, and $b$ a natural number. Assume that the universal Tate point satisfies the universal Tate equation: the Weierstrass curve `tateUnivCurve` over $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ \mathbb{Z}$, with $a_1=1$, $a_2=a_3=0$ and $a_4,a_6$ the diagonal series `tateUnivA4`, `tateUnivA6` built from the coefficients of `tateA4`, `tateA6`, has its affine equation satisfied at the explicit divisor-sum series `tateUnivX`, `tateUnivY`. Let `tateBase K p` be the Tate curve $\langle 1,0,0,\mathtt{tateA4},\mathtt{tateA6}\rangle$ over $K((q))$, obtained from its integral power-series model by coefficient reduction and then by the substitution $q \mapsto q^{p}$ (the Hahn-series ring map induced by $n \mapsto pn$ on exponents). Let $S$ be the finite set of pairs of Laurent series given by the image of $\{1,\dots,\lfloor p/2\rfloor\}$ under $k \mapsto$ the point `nonToricPoint K p (ζ ^ (b * k)) k`, i.e. the images in $K((q))$ of the two-variable slot substitutions `slotSubst K p (ζ ^ (b*k)) k` applied to `tateUnivX` and `tateUnivY`. Then the Weierstrass curve produced by the Vélu formulas from `tateBase K p` and $S$ — same $a_1,a_2,a_3$, with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4 - 5\,\mathrm{veluTSum}$ and $a_6$ by $a_6 - b_2\,\mathrm{veluTSum} - 7\,\mathrm{veluWSum}$ — coincides with the Tate curve over $K((q))$ twisted by $q \mapsto \zeta^{b} q$, that is, with the coefficientwise image of `tateLaurent K` under the ring map `qTwist (ζ ^ b)` multiplying the $q^{k}$-coefficient by $(\zeta^{b})^{k}$.
--
--   This is the formal counterpart of the classical computation that the quotient of the Tate curve with parameter $q^{p}$ by a non-toric subgroup of order $p$, generated by the point with parameter $\zeta^{b}q$, is the Tate curve with parameter $\zeta^{b}q$; the Vélu sums are evaluated as identities between divisor sums, so no division is required and $K$ may be an arbitrary commutative ring. It is used in the analysis of the $q$-expansion of the level-$p$ structure, via [`ModularCurve.LevelP.quotientByLine_tateBase_nonToricPoint_fst`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelP.quotientByLine_tateBase_nonToricPoint_fst).
